    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION The Note is convertible, subject to certain conditions, at a variable\nprice equal to 95% of the lower of (a) the daily volume-weighted average price (\u201c VWAP \u201d) of our common stock for the\ntrading day immediately preceding the date of measurement; and (b) the average daily VWAP for the common shares for the five (5) trading\ndays immediately preceding the date of measurement. Because the Conversion Shares issuable upon conversion of the Note may be issued at\nprices significantly below the book value or trading price of our common stock at the time of issuance, and because the number of shares\nissuable upon conversion increases as the price of our common stock declines, investors and existing shareholders may experience immediate\nand substantial dilution. Given the variable nature of the conversion price of the Note, the number of Conversion Shares issuable upon\nconversion of the N",
